<article class="env-remark" id="09W8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09W8">Remark <span data-tag="09W8">7.25.11</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $U \to V$ be a morphism of $\mathcal{C}$. The cocontinuous functors $\mathcal{C}/U \to \mathcal{C}$ and $j : \mathcal{C}/U \to \mathcal{C}/V$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/03EH" data-tag="03EH">7.25.8</a>) satisfy property $P$ of Remark <a href="/tag/09W7" data-tag="09W7">7.20.5</a>. For example, if we have objects $(X/U)$, $(W/V)$, a morphism $g : j(X/U) \to (W/V)$, and a covering $\{ f_ i : (W_ i/V) \to (W/V)\} $ then $(X \times _ W W_ i/U)$ is an avatar of $(X/U) \times _{g, (W/V), f_ i} (W_ i/V)$ and the family $\{ (X \times _ W W_ i/U) \to (X/U)\} $ is a covering of $\mathcal{C}/U$. </p>
</article>